Looking at the cuboid (5×2×2), the visible cubes force the assignments: the black piece is the 2×2 top block plus one cube below; the light grey piece is the front top row of three plus the bottom front corner and the hidden bottom-back corner behind it; the medium grey piece is the bottom front row plus the two hidden bottom-back cubes at the far end. That leaves the white piece with the top back row of three cubes plus the two hidden bottom-back cubes directly beneath the middle and right of that row — a flat 2×2 block with one extra cube, i.e. a P-shape.

Rotated 90°, this is exactly the shape shown in diagram E (a column of three beside a column of two, forming a 2×2 block with one extra cube).

